                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51f2018f-1625-47bf-b6c5-8ca0151c398d",
                        "source_entry_id": "db167a30-3ca7-34c2-972a-2de7fc4debf8",
                        "source_sense_description": "рабочий типографии, занятый набором",
                        "target_lang_word": "compositor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "compositor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b912d578-ee26-36d7-9473-586a3f95635c",
                                        "entry_id": "8702336d-9102-38d2-b16d-3f89fd3fe561",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who sets type; a typesetter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97438efc-4aa9-48f8-859c-119ab2e7617f",
                                                "sense_id": "b912d578-ee26-36d7-9473-586a3f95635c",
                                                "text": "Thus, when he drew up instructions in lawyer language […] his clerks […] understood him very well. If he had written a love letter, or a farce, or a ballade, or a story, no one, either clerks, or friends, or compositors, would have understood anything but a word here and a word there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ce0a0fb-b802-4c82-8a1e-eb39afd5c86d",
                                                "sense_id": "b912d578-ee26-36d7-9473-586a3f95635c",
                                                "text": "All Spaniards, we discovered, knew two English expressions. One was 'O.K., baby', the other was a word used by the Barcelona whores in their dealings with English sailors, and I am afraid the compositors would not print it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6eab2e57-75f5-4504-a74c-5091ea280fad",
                                                "sense_id": "b912d578-ee26-36d7-9473-586a3f95635c",
                                                "text": "However late medieval copyists were supervised — and controls were much more lax than many accounts suggest — scribes were incapable of committing the sort of \"standardized\" error that was produced by a compositor who dropped the word \"not\" from the Seventh Commandment and thus created the \"wicked\" Bible of 1631."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "612dee49-0ce7-3daa-b66b-dacf28bbdd72",
                                        "entry_id": "8702336d-9102-38d2-b16d-3f89fd3fe561",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who, or that which, composes or sets in order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16685826-282e-425e-801a-b81ae1265f1b",
                                                "sense_id": "612dee49-0ce7-3daa-b66b-dacf28bbdd72",
                                                "text": "I work as an image compositor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b09dff6f-1dc8-3ae3-829f-613fcf446a69",
                                        "entry_id": "8702336d-9102-38d2-b16d-3f89fd3fe561",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A system that puts images together in a buffer (such as individual windows on a desktop) to generate a final display image."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e10fd1ed-0693-4256-85c0-9070e94dc9ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "db167a30-3ca7-34c2-972a-2de7fc4debf8",
                        "source_sense_description": "рабочий типографии, занятый набором",
                        "target_lang_word": "typesetter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "typesetter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8f2effa-c26d-31a5-9fea-793f1fd80eac",
                                        "entry_id": "943a2e44-a723-36bb-a862-741d3be072b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who sets type; an employee in a printshop who manually selected pieces of movable type and assembled them for printing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "575fc9ea-57f8-4af8-b25f-b0e04389633d",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f2effa-c26d-31a5-9fea-793f1fd80eac",
                                                "text": "It’s hard to say who has the longest name in history, but a Philadelphia-area typesetter from the early 1900s chose a very long name for himself. Known, among other things, as Hubert Blaine Wolfe+590, Sr., his name has been published in many different forms since."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a994dd29-c874-4378-88a3-c532e7cc0726",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f2effa-c26d-31a5-9fea-793f1fd80eac",
                                                "text": "My writing all took place over weekends, and because I only lived about ten miles away, Peter would hot-foot it to my home on a Monday morning to collect a large parcel of hand-typed sheets of copy, for despatch to the typesetters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2e32b93-fb67-3ba9-afe4-1db9c0c6191f",
                                        "entry_id": "943a2e44-a723-36bb-a862-741d3be072b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A machine that combines type in the correct order for printing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
